{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":13689,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"239eed3b-cd38-501a-b5fe-79dd94bf5562","total_cost_usd":0.20852199999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7724,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4252,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004317,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":976,"cacheReadInputTokens":905,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7724,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.204205,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"The declaration names limpet_id as the independent-unit column; the frozen data show 12 distinct tags (LP01-LP12), each appearing exactly 4 times (once per trial_no 1-4) with constant shore_zone and shell_length_mm within a tag, matching the description of repeated readings of the same individual. Each limpet belongs to exactly one procedure arm (LP01-LP06 low, LP07-LP12 high), so the unit column is consistent across both arms of the two-sample comparison.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: the summary table reports 6 animals per zone with 24 measurements and 4 ramps per animal, the Analysis section states 'Every measurement in the file was entered into the test as one observation of its group', and the selected result reports t(46) with n = 24 per group, confirming all 48 non-independent repeated measurements were entered into scipy.stats.ttest_ind (a row-independent procedure) as independent observations rather than one value per limpet (which would give df = 10).\",\"The report itself asserts 'All 48 measurements were treated as independent observations, giving 46 degrees of freedom', which directly demonstrates pseudoreplication relative to the declared independent unit limpet_id.\",\"The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['limpet_id'], which follows directly from the declaration's independent-unit column; the lock's stated authority limitations correctly confine it to the case, input digest, procedure, and ordered key without asserting numerical or scientific correctness.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declaration names limpet_id as the independent-unit column; the frozen data show 12 distinct tags (LP01-LP12), each appearing exactly 4 times (once per trial_no 1-4) with constant shore_zone and shell_length_mm within a tag, matching the description of repeated readings of the same individual. Each limpet belongs to exactly one procedure arm (LP01-LP06 low, LP07-LP12 high), so the unit column is consistent across both arms of the two-sample comparison.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: the summary table reports 6 animals per zone with 24 measurements and 4 ramps per animal, the Analysis section states 'Every measurement in the file was entered into the test as one observation of its group', and the selected result reports t(46) with n = 24 per group, confirming all 48 non-independent repeated measurements were entered into scipy.stats.ttest_ind (a row-independent procedure) as independent observations rather than one value per limpet (which would give df = 10).","The report itself asserts 'All 48 measurements were treated as independent observations, giving 46 degrees of freedom', which directly demonstrates pseudoreplication relative to the declared independent unit limpet_id.","The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['limpet_id'], which follows directly from the declaration's independent-unit column; the lock's stated authority limitations correctly confine it to the case, input digest, procedure, and ordered key without asserting numerical or scientific correctness."]},"ttft_ms":6500,"ttft_stream_ms":1988,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":12613,"uuid":"ad9d71fe-2ece-4ea3-bd93-d11a34ba9dab"}
